From effbd5a4fc4514cd9d7aa263a5fc4dc48b1fe89e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 23:14:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] C-81 (Codex M01): rollback is decided durably on the
 PROMOTED row, executed idempotently, verified, and only then REVERTED

cells.mark_rollback_pending / note_rollback_attempt / revert(verified=...) make REVERTED the
completion of a rollback rather than its start. runner.monitor_trials resumes a pending
rollback on every pass instead of re-judging it; VERIFIERS read the active job-priority policy
(registry incumbent and swarm.orchestrate.priority_policy) or the dropped floor before the row
may say reverted. The rollback incident opens while pending and resolves only on verification.
enforce.drop_floor is idempotent. Proven by a handler-level test that kills the process before
the executor and again between executor and verification, then restarts.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
